# BUIM — Bespoke User Interface Manager

**BUIM** is a lightweight, zero-dependency, local-storage-backed floating UI manager. Originally designed for Eschaton projects and GeoFS, it provides an easy way to build structured, floating settings menus with built-in state management.

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

To use BUIM, simply inject or include the provided JavaScript in your environment. Once the script runs, it attaches itself to `window.BUIM`.

Wait for the DOM to load or listen for the `BUIMLoaded` event before initializing your menus:

```javascript
document.addEventListener("BUIMLoaded", () => {
  // Initialize your UI here
});
```

---

## 🛠 Basic Usage

BUIM operates on the concept of **Sections**. A Section is an expandable container inside the floating menu. Each section manages its own `localStorage` prefix to prevent key collisions.

```javascript
// 1. Create a new Section
// BUIM(DisplayName, LocalStoragePrefix)
const myMods = new BUIM("My Cool Mod", "myMod_");

// 2. Chain methods to build your UI
myMods
  .addHeader(4, "General Settings")
  .addItem("Enable feature X", "featureX", "checkbox", true)
  .addItem("Max Speed", "maxSpeed", "number", 100)
  .addDropdown("Theme", "theme", { "Dark Mode": "dark", "Light Mode": "light" }, "dark")
  .addButton("Apply Now", () => console.log("Applied!"));

// 3. Read values later
if (myMods.isEnabled && myMods.getBool("featureX")) {
  console.log("Feature X is active with speed:", myMods.get("maxSpeed"));
}
```

---

## 📚 API Reference

### Global API (`window.BUIM`)

The `BUIM` object acts as both the Section constructor and a global event emitter.

*   `new BUIM(name, prefix)`: Creates and returns a new `Section` instance.
*   `BUIM.toggle()`: Programmatically opens or closes the BUIM menu.
*   `BUIM.on(event, callback)`: Listen to global events.
    *   *Supported events:* `"menu:open"`, `"menu:close"`
*   `BUIM.emit(event, data)`: Emit a global custom event.

### Section API (Instance Methods)

All UI-building methods are **chainable** (they return `this`).

#### Building the UI

*   **`addItem(description, lsName, type, defaultValue)`**
    Adds a text, number, or checkbox input.
    *   `type`: `"text" | "number" | "checkbox"` (Defaults to `"text"`).
*   **`addDropdown(description, lsName, options, defaultValue)`**
    Adds a dropdown select menu.
    *   `options`: An object formatted as `{ "Visible Label": "storedValue" }`.
*   **`addButton(label, onClick)`**
    Adds a clickable button.
*   **`addHeader(level, text)`**
    Adds a visual heading inside the section (level corresponds to `h2`, `h3`, etc.).
*   **`addShortcut(description, lsName, defaultValue, onKeyDown, [onKeyUp])`**
    Adds a customizable keyboard shortcut binder. Users can click it to record a new key combination.
    *   `defaultValue`: Key code (e.g., `"KeyG"` or encoded string `"KeyG&,true&,false&,false&,false"`).

#### State & Data Management

Keys passed to these methods (`lsName`) are automatically prefixed with the Section's prefix.

*   **`get(lsName)`**: Returns the stored string value.
*   **`getBool(lsName)`**: Returns `true` or `false` (useful for checkboxes).
*   **`set(lsName, value)`**: Programmatically updates a value in `localStorage` and visually updates the UI element if it exists.
*   **`isEnabled`**: (Getter) Returns a boolean indicating if the Section's master toggle switch (in the header) is checked.

#### Section Events

You can listen to events scoped strictly to your section:

```javascript
myMods.on("toggle", (isEnabled) => {
  console.log("Master switch toggled:", isEnabled);
});

myMods.on("reset", () => {
  console.log("User clicked RESET DEFAULTS");
});
```

---

## ⌨️ Keyboard Shortcuts

The `addShortcut` method comes with a built-in macro recorder. When a user clicks the shortcut button in the menu, it listens for their next keystroke (including modifier keys like Ctrl/Shift/Alt) and saves it securely to `localStorage`.

```javascript
myMods.addShortcut(
  "Trigger Boost", 
  "boostKey", 
  "KeyB", // Default key
  (e) => { console.log("Boost key pressed!", e); },
  (e) => { console.log("Boost key released!", e); }
);
```